    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēclārātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		declaro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a making clear</i> or <i>evident, a
				disclosure, exposition, declaration</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animi tui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 10, 5, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amoris tui?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 15, 21, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub eadem declaratione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 30 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ps. 118, 130</span></i>.</div>
